v^{(l)}_{j}(x,t) = \overline{v^{(l)}_{j}(x,-t)}
\end{equation*}
for $(x,t) \in \mathcal{O}^{(j)} \times (-T, 0)$. In turn, this requires the boundary data $f^{(j)}_{l}$ to be real-valued.

