\label{main_theorem_other_setting}
Let $\Omega$ be a smooth bounded domain in $\mathbb{R}^{n}\;(n = 2, 3)$. Consider $\Gamma_{j}\;(j = 1,2)$ relatively open subsets of $\partial\Omega$ and let $\mathcal{O}^{(j)} \subset \Omega$ be a relatively open neighborhood of $\partial \Omega$ such that $\partial \mathcal{O}^{(j)} \setminus \partial\Omega$ is $C^{2}$. For \eqref{two_component_GPEqn_small_initial_data}, suppose we have real-valued $f^{(j)}_{l} \in H^{4}(\Omega) \cap H^{3}_{0}(\Omega)$ and the conditions in \eqref{coefficient_smallness_assumption_1}-\eqref{coefficient_assumption_0} satisfied. \\ \indent
Then, for $j \in \{1,2\}$, there exists $\delta_{*,j} > 0$ such that when
\begin{equation}
\delta_{j,\Gamma_{j}} \coloneqq \left\Vert \partial_t\left(\partial^{3}_{\epsilon_{1}\epsilon_{2}\epsilon_{3}}\partial_{\nu}(u_{j,1}-u_{j,2})\Big|_{\epsilon_{1} = \epsilon_{2} = \epsilon_{3} = 0}\right) \right\Vert_{L^{2}(\Gamma_{j} \times (0, T))} \leq \delta_{*,j},
