we have
\begin{equation}
\left \Vert \tilde{q}_{j,1} - \tilde{q}_{j,2} \right \Vert^{2}_{L^{2}(\Omega\setminus\mathcal{O}^{(j)})} \leq C_{j}\left[\left(\ln \left(\delta_{j,\Gamma_{j}}^{-1}\right) \right)^{-1} + \delta_{j,\Gamma_{j}}\right]
\end{equation}
for a constant $C_{j} = C_{j}\left(\Omega, \Gamma_{j}, \mathcal{O}^{(j)}, M_{0}, M_{1}, M_{2}, T, \gamma_{-}, \gamma_{+} \right) > 0$.

